<!DOCTYPE softwarelist SYSTEM "softwarelist.dtd">
<!--
license:CC0-1.0

    Roland PCM cards for the JD-800 and the JD-990, taken as the mask ROM
    reads.  Both series go in the same slot and wear the same line swap as
    the SR-JV80 boards, which the slot undoes; the SO-PCM1 cards carry the
    JV-80 header the boards do, the SO-JD80 cards the JD-800 one.  The two
    2 MB cards fill the bank above their own as well.

    Each entry is commented with the card's own label and with the build
    date stamped after it, both read from the descrambled image; the year
    is that build date rather than the date of sale.  The descriptions are
    the sixteen-character names the JV-1080 firmware keeps for the cards it
    knows, and the cards it does not know are listed by part number alone
    rather than guessed at.

    Not dumped: SO-PCM1-05 (Accordion).
-->

